# A named Structure needs no closer and no return (the author, Q54 and its clarification; book §9, :559: a head that
# resolves to nothing, with a Structure tail, declares one): Counter's first item is an executable statement and
# only the dedent ends it.  Declaring it runs nothing (hits 0), a call runs its body once (hits 1).  It was refused
# (its items read as a statement's: "unknown field path root", in a method "a call path must end at a callable
# field").
# At the root, walked: a 0, b 1 -- success 7; any other 64.
int: hits 0
fn: peek () int
    return: node\hits
end: peek
Counter:
    node\hits: node\hits + 1
    size_t: n 0U
int: a 0
a: peek()
Counter
int: b 0
b: peek()
int: r 64
if: a = 0 && b = 1
    r: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: r; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
